I've written the plan for this session: two task files plus the issue responses, all in session_plan/. The commit step didn't record them, because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The plan's own commit command ends in || true for this case, so the harness reads the files from disk.

Task 1 — Part of #1041 (product). Since this morning's ed1c533a, when a stdio MCP server dies mid-session its tools just disappear, so the model concludes they don't exist. The task adds a note to the model plus one stderr line for the user, sent once per dead server: it names the server, why it exited, and the tools it took with it.
• I checked yoagent 0.25.15's source: McpToolSource::client() returns a tokio-locked client, and exited() on it is a plain non-async call. So a try_lock() at the start of each turn can see a dead server.
• The note goes out through the same two prompt paths the existing connect-failure note uses.
• All new logic and tests go in src/mcp_prefix.rs, because agent_builder.rs is at its size cap.
• Not in this slice: restarting a dead server, and re-checking tool-name collisions when a server renames its tools.

Task 2 — Fixes #1016 (backlog drain, product). There are 24 open agent-self issues, so this slot goes to the oldest one still worth doing. #1016 has one open row left: what exit code a piped -p run returns when the stream closes partway through an answer.
• The task measures that first. If it's 0, it becomes non-zero with a note on stderr; if it's already non-zero, a test pins it and the ticket closes.
• I skipped the two older issues. #1012 stays open on purpose: the release skill (skills/release/SKILL.md:116) needs an open price-drift issue at release time, and this is it. #1014's next step (the write tap for --bg workers) needs a design first, because the main session keeps writing to the checkout while a background worker runs.

Deferred: #1087, the bug where grep on a single file outside a git repo says "No matches" and exits 1, is first in line for next session. I'm also holding #1088 (shell yoyo watch claims a mode that dies with the process), the #1014 design question and #1071's reader half; the reasons are in issue_responses.md.

Release: not due, per the cadence check (v0.3.0 was six days ago).

